INTERNSHIP DS WORK

DecodeLabs Data Science Internship - project work.

## Project 2: Fraud Detection Pipeline (Supervised Learning)

Notebook: project2.ipynb

Builds a leak-free classification pipeline for the Kaggle credit card
fraud dataset (284,807 transactions, 0.17% fraud) using SMOTE inside
imblearn.pipeline.Pipeline, 5-fold StratifiedKFold GridSearchCV, and
Precision/Recall/ROC-AUC evaluation on an untouched test set (no
Accuracy metric, per assignment spec). SMOTE and scaling are applied
only within each training fold, never before the train/test split.

- Logistic Regression: tuned and evaluated successfully.
  Best CV ROC-AUC: 0.9816 (C=0.01, smote__k_neighbors=3).
- Random Forest: the pipeline and GridSearchCV are implemented
  correctly (no data leakage, no scaler on the tree model, 5-fold CV,
  preprocessing tuned jointly with the model), but the hyperparameter
  search could not be completed on the available hardware. SMOTE
  balances each training fold to the majority class, which for this
  dataset means fitting on several hundred thousand rows per fit; even
  a single shallow tree took multiple seconds to fit. The full grid
  search still did not finish in a practical amount of time after
  removing nested parallelism, bounding max_depth, fixing
  smote__k_neighbors to a single value, and tuning on a 40k-row
  stratified subsample instead of the full ~227k-row training set.
  No Random Forest results are reported in this submission - this is
  a compute constraint, not a gap in the modeling approach. The RF
  cells are left in the notebook as implemented and would complete
  given stronger hardware (more CPU cores) or a smaller search budget.
